fact WorkItem(id: "WI-559", description: some(value: "SetLiteral / TupleLiteral occurrence-build drops all elements (pre-existing; surfaced by WI-027 code review). The term->occurrence build arms for 'SetLiteral' and 'TupleLiteral' in node_occurrence.rs visit_fn still use collect_list_visits(kb, Some(t)) -> list_to_vec, a cons/nil spine walker that returns EMPTY for these functors (their elements live in pos_args for SetLiteral, named_args for TupleLiteral — NOT a cons/nil spine). Result: Expr::SetLit([]) / Expr::TupleLit{empty} — every element silently dropped (loud-over-silent violation). WI-027 fixed the IDENTICAL bug for ListLiteral (read pos_args directly) but deliberately left the siblings to keep scope tight. ALSO: try_occurrence_to_term gained a ListLit reify arm (-> ListLiteral term twin) but SetLit/TupleLit still fall to '_ => None' -> occurrence_to_term debug_assert/Bottom, so a set/tuple literal reaching reify hits the assert (debug) or silent Bottom (release). Fix: (a) SetLiteral build reads pos_args (mirror ListLiteral); (b) TupleLiteral build reads named_args (its element carrier per convert.rs); (c) add SetLit + TupleLit arms to try_occurrence_to_term reifying to anthill.reflect.SetLiteral / TupleLiteral term twins (TupleLit via named_args). ALSO note (separate, lower pri): a ListLiteral with a 'tail:' named arg ([h|t] surface) is dropped at occurrence-build because Expr::ListLit has no tail slot — the resolver's bounded_list_elements DOES chase a ListLiteral tail, so the term round-trip disagrees with the SLD view (latent dedup-collision for [h|t] literals); fixing needs an Expr::ListLit representation change or a cons/nil desugar of head-tail literals. Acceptance: a {a,b} set literal and (a,b) tuple literal round-trip through occurrence_to_term without dropping elements; cargo-test green; add a focused round-trip test per literal kind."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-24T10:20:17Z"))

